# A guest throws the box to another guest, who grabs it in flight: a grab of a body flying under
# another guest. The host grants it on the seam's contact evidence (her character along the path
# the host took of it, the box put back along its velocity to her grab's tick), the box rides her
# hand on every endpoint, and the thrower's states of the flight sent before she heard of the catch
# are dropped by their number.
scenario catch_guest_throw_100
scene four_chars_item
seed 31
guests 2
settle 6s

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 10ms loss 1%
net g2 rtt 100ms jitter 10ms loss 1%

p1 grab box as lift
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 4 0.2 0 speed 9 as throw
# The walk ends the tick the box comes within her reach on her own world, and the grab follows.
p2 walk box speed 1 on throw as reach
p2 grab box as catch
# Held long enough for her hand to reach the thrower's world: two one-way trips and two delays.
p2 wait 1500ms
p2 drop as put

expect result lift granted
expect result throw done
expect result catch granted
expect held box p2
expect agree_at_rest 5cm
expect no_stuck
# The thrower simulates the flight on until the grant reaches her, a state a tick: at least one
# arrives late. Measured 7 over 20 seeds (seed 31: 7); at most a state a tick over the grant's trip
# to her and a lost record's resend, as in recall_flight.
expect late_drops.count >= 1
expect late_drops.count <= 30
# Derived: the claim takes over from the pose the catcher shows (as in throw_catch): 0, and 1 cm
# for a placement's rounding.
expect local_correction.max <= 1cm
# The host's copy stops where the thrower's states end at the grant and hands over to her hand at
# her first state through the render offset (the jump counted from the tick the owner changes):
# measured 0.16-0.17 m over 20 seeds in both modes, against 0.23 m for a catch of the host's own
# throw at this speed (throw_catch at 9 m/s). The stub draws a copy at its newest state with no
# offset, so the handover shows whole: measured up to 0.86 m, no snap.
expect jump.max <= 0.2m stub 1m
expect snap.count <= 0
# A catch is a grab: nothing moves by interaction, and nothing of the host's touches the flight.
expect takes.count <= 0
expect take_refusals.count <= 0
expect reclaims.count <= 0
